{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":298828,"ns":0,"title":"Affine group","extract":"In mathematics, the affine group or general affine group of any affine space is the group of all invertible affine transformations from the space into itself.  In the case of a Euclidean space (where the associated field of scalars is the real numbers), the affine group consists of those functions from the space to itself such that the image of every line is a line.","description":"Group of all affine transformations of an affine space","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}